I built the Turnstile widget request for the `demo-signup-form` widget in account `demo`, in managed mode, for `demo.example`, `localhost`, and `127.0.0.1`. The tool ran as a dry run, so nothing was created and I have no real sitekey or secret yet.

**Frontend** (inside the signup form, next to the existing inputs):

```html
<script src="https://challenges.cloudflare.com/turnstile/v0/api.js" async defer></script>
<div class="cf-turnstile" data-sitekey="<SITEKEY>" data-action="signup"></div>
```

**Server** (in the signup handler, before the existing logic runs). Set `TURNSTILE_SECRET` in the environment and `TURNSTILE_HOSTNAMES=demo.example` in production. Leave `localhost` out of the production value:

```js
const token = req.body['cf-turnstile-response'];
const expectedHostnames = new Set((process.env.TURNSTILE_HOSTNAMES ?? '').split(',').map((h) => h.trim()).filter(Boolean));
if (typeof token !== 'string' || !token || token.length > 2048 || expectedHostnames.size === 0) {
  return res.status(403).send('forbidden');
}
let result;
try {
  const r = await fetch('https://challenges.cloudflare.com/turnstile/v0/siteverify', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded' },
    signal: AbortSignal.timeout(10_000),
    body: new URLSearchParams({ secret: process.env.TURNSTILE_SECRET, response: token, remoteip: req.ip }),
  });
  if (!r.ok) throw new Error(`siteverify ${r.status}`);
  result = await r.json();
} catch {
  return res.status(403).send('forbidden');
}
if (!result.success || result.action !== 'signup' || !expectedHostnames.has(result.hostname)) {
  return res.status(403).send('forbidden');
}
// existing signup logic runs here, unchanged
```

I did not find or edit your signup form, since the repo I have open is the MCP positioning demo and does not contain a `demo.example` signup handler. Once you point me at that code, I can insert the snippets. Also, the widget has not been validated end to end: I still need the real secret, a live token on the running backend, and a check that replaying the token is rejected.

I created a dry-run Turnstile widget request for `demo.example`, `localhost`, and `127.0.0.1` and wrote the frontend embed and the server-side Siteverify check. Nothing was sent to Cloudflare and no code in the repo was changed.
